# Shared build context for every Dockerfile in this repo (backends/apps/sms-gateway,
# backends/apps/sms-worker, admin) — all three build from the repo root, because
# include_server_schema! needs schema/ and the pnpm workspace needs
# frontends/packages/. This file keeps that root context small; without it, `target/`
# and `node_modules/` alone turn a multi-second `docker build` context
# upload into a multi-minute one.

# Rust — `target/` alone matches only the root; the four workspace-excluded
# manifests (sdks/rust, examples/rust, ci/e2e-integration, deploy/backup-tool)
# each keep their own `target/` one level down, and a plain `COPY . .` in
# every builder stage dragged all of them into the image. Found when
# `just demo` filled a 96 GB disk copying `examples/rust/target/debug/deps`.
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Node / pnpm — node_modules can exist at the root and per-package
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.turbo/
**/.next/
**/dist/
# generated at build time inside the image, never from the host — see
# frontends/packages/sms-client/GENERATING.md
frontends/packages/sms-client/src/
frontends/packages/sms-client/dist/

# VCS / editor / OS
.git/
.gitignore
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local env files — never bake secrets into an image layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
deploy/.env
deploy/.env.*
!deploy/.env.example

# Production-readiness audit (review round 1, item 4): deploy/secrets/
# holds the real console-private-key.pem/console-client-id/rclone.conf
# every deployed operator provisions locally — every image in this repo
# builds with `context: ..` (the repo root), so without this rule those
# real secrets would enter the build context (and, worse, any image
# layer that happens to COPY the context wholesale) the moment they
# exist on disk. `.gitignore` already keeps them out of the repository
# itself; this keeps them out of a build context too.
deploy/secrets/*
!deploy/secrets/.gitkeep
!deploy/secrets/*.example

# Docs and CI artifacts not needed inside a build context
docs/
.github/
*.md
!README.md
